        <body>
            <div xml:id="d601">

                <pb facs="0514" n="432" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg432"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/980.</note>
                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-03-23"><hi rendition="#italic">March 23,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 440.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 16th instant, by which you advise the Department
                    that Col, Manuel Tamborrell, commanding your Government’s forces <pb facs="0515"
                        n="433" xml:id="pg433"/> at Ciudad Juarez, states in an official report that
                    about February 7 several groups of persons on the American side of the Rio
                    Grande near that city fired on the command of Lieut. Col. Manuel G. Pueblita of
                    the Mexican Army.</p>
                <p>Copies of your note have been sent to the War Department and the Department of
                    Justice for their information and for appropriate action by the Attorney
                    General.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.],</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
